{"nodes": [{"id": "blocks_http_compile_read", "label": "compile_read (public http entry / mode dispatcher)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L434-L569", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "compile_flow.py always calls this one name regardless of block.mode, so read/write/lookup dispatch happens inside it rather than at the caller."}, {"id": "blocks_http_compile_write", "label": "_compile_write (POST/PUT/PATCH write mode)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L993-L1161", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "writeForwards chooses which InvokeHTTP relationship continues the chain: 'original' forwards the pre-POST record untouched, 'response' routes Response through read mode's own _parse_response chain."}, {"id": "blocks_http_compile_lookup", "label": "_compile_lookup (GET enrichment, response reshaped under joinField)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L1164-L1234", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Honest limitation: NiFi has no join primitive in scope, so the 'merge' is implemented by reshaping the RESPONSE under /<joinField>_lookup rather than a true two-flowfile-lineage merge back onto the parent record."}, {"id": "blocks_http_build_pagination", "label": "_build_pagination (page_meta -> has_more -> next loop builder)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L707-L812", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "loop_target is parameterised so read mode loops back to `fetch` while write mode loops back to `render_body` (write's InvokeHTTP holds no per-page state; the body must be re-rendered from the updated counters)."}, {"id": "blocks_http_pagination_init_props", "label": "_pagination_init_props (mode-agnostic counter seeding)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L234-L258", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The counters (offset/limit, page/page_size, cursor, page_count) are identical in read and write mode; only WHERE the resulting EL is embedded differs, so the seeding function is shared verbatim."}, {"id": "blocks_http_build_query", "label": "_build_query (pagination counters -> URL query string)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L212-L231", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "blocks_http_auto_fill_pagination_body", "label": "_auto_fill_pagination_body (pagination counters -> JSON request body)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L943-L990", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Mechanically a text splice, not a JSON parse: the template legitimately holds non-JSON EL tokens (a bare ${offset}) until NiFi evaluates it, so a json.loads/dumps round-trip would corrupt them. Only offset/page pairs are spliced, which is exactly why cursor pagination cannot work in write mode."}, {"id": "blocks_http_parse_response", "label": "_parse_response (json/csv/xml -> (record_tail, original_tail))", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L353-L431", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SplitJson was picked over SplitXml so csv and xml share one downstream code path; every format lands on the same per-record JSON shape the rest of the compiler assumes."}, {"id": "blocks_http_apply_columnar_transform", "label": "_apply_columnar_transform (Jolt shift: positional rows -> named objects)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L316-L350", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Without it SplitJson yields per-row FlowFiles whose content is a bare JSON array; every downstream EvaluateJsonPath silently finds nothing (Path Not Found Behavior: ignore) so records flow through dedup/publish looking clean while carrying no usable fields."}, {"id": "blocks_http_sanitize_columnar_field_name", "label": "_sanitize_columnar_field_name", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L303-L313", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Column names come from a caller-supplied list (column-oriented rows carry no field names at runtime); sanitized so one name is simultaneously safe as a Jolt output key, an EvaluateJsonPath property name and an Avro field name."}, {"id": "blocks_http_apply_auth", "label": "_apply_auth (six auth modes onto InvokeHTTP props)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L148-L209", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "M16: a query-location api_key must go in the URL, never a dynamic property \u2014 InvokeHTTP emits every dynamic property as a request HEADER, which would be malformed AND leak the secret into a second location."}, {"id": "blocks_http_base_url_expr", "label": "_base_url_expr (service base URL or APISIX proxy swap)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L124-L135", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "blocks_http_normalize_path", "label": "_normalize_path (baseUrl+path join safety)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L101-L121", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "User-reported live failure: blind {baseUrl}{path} concatenation produced invalid hosts like dummyjson.comhttps / dummyjson.comusers."}, {"id": "blocks_http_build_session_login", "label": "_build_session_login (one ExecuteGroovyScript login step)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L645-L700", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "R3: the previous ReplaceText-body + InvokeHTTP + EvaluateJsonPath chain was proven undeployable \u2014 NiFi refuses a #{sensitive param} reference inside a non-sensitive STATIC property, and sensitiveDynamicPropertyNames cannot cover a static descriptor. Only a SENSITIVE DYNAMIC property (ExecuteGroovyScript's binding mechanism) can legally carry the password."}, {"id": "blocks_http_groovy_session_login_script", "label": "GROOVY_SESSION_LOGIN_SCRIPT", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L594-L642", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Credential JSON-escaping happens in-script via JsonOutput.toJson, never string concatenation; TOKEN_PATH is a literal dot-path split, no regex."}, {"id": "blocks_http_session_header_value", "label": "_session_header_value (tokenTemplate -> ${session.token})", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L138-L145", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "blocks_http_el_field_refs", "label": "_el_field_refs (record fields referenced in a path/body template)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L831-L841", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "blocks_http_el_builtin_deny", "label": "_EL_BUILTIN_DENY (built-in ${...} tokens excluded from promotion)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L825-L828", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately a small explicit set rather than clever pattern matching, so we never try to JsonPath a flowfile's own uuid or a pagination counter out of record content."}, {"id": "blocks_http_extract_fields", "label": "_extract_fields (promote record fields to flowfile attributes)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L844-L940", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "preserve_existing=True adds a per-field present/missing RouteOnAttribute gate for chained reads: the old single multi-property EvaluateJsonPath could overwrite an inherited attribute with an empty value, producing URLs like /sites//assets."}, {"id": "blocks_http_probe_path", "label": "_probe_path (recordPath[*] -> recordPath[0] probe)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L261-L265", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "blocks_http_ensure_csv_reader", "label": "_ensure_csv_reader (CSVReader CS, infer-schema)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L268-L281", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "infer-schema rather than the reference flows' schema-name strategy \u2014 an ad-hoc http response has no registered Avro schema to bind to."}, {"id": "blocks_http_ensure_xml_reader", "label": "_ensure_xml_reader (XMLReader CS, infer-schema)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L284-L297", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "blocks_http_build_trigger", "label": "_build_trigger (GenerateFlowFile root seed)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L572-L579", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "blocks_http_service_for", "label": "_service_for (resolve block.serviceId)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L92-L98", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "blocks_http_invoke_http_baseline", "label": "_INVOKE_HTTP_BASELINE (shared InvokeHTTP property baseline)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L68-L87", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pins 'Request Content-Type': '${mime.type}', which is precisely why write-mode pagination must restore mime.type on every loop iteration."}, {"id": "blocks_http_c4_el_single_pass", "label": "C4: EL must live on the processor property NiFi evaluates", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L514-L525", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "NiFi EL is single-pass: an EL template STORED IN AN ATTRIBUTE is never re-evaluated. So offset/page/cursor put the counter-bearing URL template directly on fetch's 'HTTP URL' property, while none/next_url have a concrete URL that can safely be frozen into the request.url attribute (next overwrites it for next_url)."}, {"id": "blocks_http_write_mode_pagination_styles", "label": "Write-mode pagination supports only offset/page; cursor and next_url rejected", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L1041-L1057", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both other styles COMPILE but produce a loop that never advances and re-POSTs page 1 forever: next_url sets the request.url attribute that only read mode's fetch reads, and cursor never reaches the body because _auto_fill_pagination_body splices offset/page pairs only. The compiler now agrees with what PaginationFields.tsx already hides."}, {"id": "blocks_http_counters_in_query_and_body", "label": "Write mode emits pagination counters in BOTH query string and body", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L1096-L1116", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The original body-only design was wrong: FortiSIEM /query/cmdb (verified live) returns byte-identical rows for body {\"start\":0} vs {\"start\":3} but different pages for ?start=0 vs ?start=3. Sending a paging parameter an API ignores is inert; failing to send one it reads is silent data corruption."}, {"id": "blocks_http_mime_type_loop_reset", "label": "mime.type reset on every write-mode loop iteration", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L1147-L1159", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "init seeds mime.type once, but the loop flowfile comes off write's Response relationship and InvokeHTTP overwrites mime.type with the RESPONSE's Content-Type. With the baseline's 'Request Content-Type': '${mime.type}', page 2 onward would POST JSON advertised as whatever the API replied with. ReplaceText cannot set attributes, so the reset belongs on `next`."}, {"id": "blocks_http_original_tail_pagination_decoupling", "label": "original_tail: pagination-continue decoupled from per-record processing", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L405-L431", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SplitJson's `split` relationship feeds the record chain while `original` (or a second connection off the InvokeHTTP Response when not splitting) feeds page_meta. With a columnar transform the original_tail is deliberately forked PRE-Jolt, since the shift keeps only rowsField and would drop sibling keys like totalCount that the stop condition reads."}], "edges": [{"source": "blocks_http_compile_read", "target": "blocks_http_compile_write", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L444-L446", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "blocks_http_compile_read", "target": "blocks_http_compile_lookup", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L447-L449", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "blocks_http_compile_read", "target": "blocks_http_build_query", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L506", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "blocks_http_compile_read", "target": "blocks_http_pagination_init_props", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L525", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "blocks_http_compile_read", "target": "blocks_http_parse_response", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L559-L562", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "blocks_http_compile_read", "target": "blocks_http_build_pagination", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L565-L567", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "blocks_http_compile_read", "target": "blocks_http_base_url_expr", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L507", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "blocks_http_compile_read", "target": "blocks_http_normalize_path", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L463", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "blocks_http_compile_read", "target": "blocks_http_el_field_refs", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L486", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "blocks_http_compile_read", "target": "blocks_http_extract_fields", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L494-L497", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "blocks_http_compile_read", "target": "blocks_http_build_session_login", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/blocks_http.py", "source_location": "L536", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "blocks_http_compile_read", "target": "blocks_http_apply_auth", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "backend/services/adapter/compiler/block